# RULE: Legacy Feature Coverage

This is a mandatory Cursor rule.

The rewrite must not lose any legacy feature from the audited softphone.

## Source Of Truth

Legacy parity is tracked in:

```txt
docs/softphone/Legacy-Feature-Coverage.md
```

Every legacy feature has an `LF-XXX` ID.

All IDs from `LF-001` through `LF-090` must be implemented or explicitly deprecated by ADR.

## Before Implementation

Before code changes identify:

- affected `LF-XXX` IDs
- current roadmap phase
- bounded context
- old modules from the audit
- acceptance focus
- target Use Cases
- target Domain Events
- tests required

If no `LF-XXX` is affected, confirm the work is platform foundation or documentation.

## No Feature Loss

Never remove or skip:

- SIP-only auth mode
- incoming call behavior
- outgoing call behavior
- hold/mute/transfer/DTMF behavior
- post-call workflows
- call history
- logging and diagnostics
- headset controls
- settings
- host API compatibility

without an ADR.

## Migration Evidence

For every completed `LF-XXX`, leave evidence:

- implementation path
- tests
- affected Use Cases
- affected Domain Events
- UX state when user-visible
- compatibility notes when external

## Coverage Check

Before finishing a task verify:

- no affected `LF-XXX` was missed
- aggregate Feature Registry entry references the legacy IDs
- acceptance focus is covered
- SIP-only telephony is not broken by removed legacy integration

## ADR Requirement

Create an ADR before:

- dropping a legacy feature
- changing legacy behavior intentionally
- replacing a legacy contract
- changing reconnect semantics
- removing a UI flow
- removing a host API method
